Linear A corpus (data/linear-a/corpus.json)
  Builds on SigLA (https://sigla.phis.me), by Ester Salgarella and Simon Castellan, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and on
  lineara.xyz (https://github.com/mwenge/lineara.xyz), by Rob Hogan, which states no licence. Our corrections and
  added layers are CC BY 4.0; the underlying texts keep their sources' terms.

SigLA sign list (data/linear-a/sigla-sign-map.json)
  SigLA's sign list (https://sigla.phis.me), by Ester Salgarella and Simon Castellan, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, with Unicode
  fields added under CC BY 4.0. The SigLA images it names are not in this repository.

Semitic root reflexes (data/semitic-roots/semitic_roots.json)
  903 reflexes come from Adam Anderson and Jason Moser, Protosemitic Root Derivations (2024), Zenodo,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.14160276, CC BY 4.0; each cites it. The consonant correspondences
  (data/semitic-roots/semitic_correspondences.json) follow Huehnergard 2019, Table 3.2 (p. 51), as cited facts.

Akkadian literary glossary (data/ane/akkadian_literary.jsonl)
  From ORACC CAMS/GKAB, CC0 1.0.

Persons and Names of the Middle Kingdom, version 6 (data/ane/pnm-v6/)
  Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.15806808, CC BY 4.0.

Prosopographia Memphitica (data/ane/prosopographia-memphitica/)
  Anne Herzberg-Beiersdorf, Prosopographia Memphitica, Humboldt-Universität zu Berlin, release 2024-11-15, Zenodo,
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.3856410, CC BY 4.0 and ODC-By 1.0.

Gauthier, Dictionnaire des noms géographiques, t. 1-6 (data/ane/gauthier-dng/)
  Henri Gauthier, Le Caire 1925-1929, public domain.

Kassite name concordances (data/ane/kassite-concordances/)
  The name indexes of Clay (YOS 1, 1912; BE A 14 and 15, 1906; PBS 2/2, 1912), Hinke (BE D 4, 1907), Radau
  (BE A 17/1, 1908) and King (Babylonian Boundary-Stones, 1912), public domain.

Pleiades places (data/ane/place-authorities/pleiades_places.jsonl)
  Pleiades (https://pleiades.stoa.org), CC BY 3.0.

ORAEC/TLA Egyptian documents (data/share-alike/egyptian/)
  ORAEC republication of Thesaurus Linguae Aegyptiae records, CC BY-SA 4.0. Anything derived from these files
  carries the same terms.

TLA v18 names (data/share-alike/tla-v18-names/)
  Thesaurus Linguae Aegyptiae, Original Earlier Egyptian sentences, corpus v18, premium, v1.1, 2024-02-16, ed. T. S.
  Richter and D. A. Werning (BBAW) and H.-W. Fischer-Elfert and P. Dils (SAW). Thesaurus Linguae Aegyptiae Lemmata in
  Wikidata 2024. The TLA's January 2018 extract in TEI (aed-tei, Simon D. Schweitzer). All CC BY-SA 4.0. Anything
  derived from these files carries the same terms.

Trismegistos Geo places (data/share-alike/trismegistos/)
  Trismegistos Geo, CC BY-SA 4.0. Anything derived from these files carries the same terms.

